body:
Legal I2 S0 on Central, 2026-11-27, recorded by Opus2. This adds to the LEGAL-WINDOW ENTRY in central-cargo-memory-budget-rev16-2026-11-22.

Fable2 #8224 set a ONE-OFF admission floor of 22,020,096 KiB for I2 S0 only, in place of ruling (c)'s 25,165,824. Two things prompted it:
- the first window's row 1 was refused at 25,100,380 KiB, 07:33:10Z;
- Central's busy baseline had drifted to about 24-26M with pairs running.

Measured in window 07:38:14Z-08:53:14Z, all three rows exit 0, no refusals:
- cold one-job `cargo build --lib` of rincon-verify: 181 s; admitted at about 24.95M; low 23,242,080 KiB (a drawdown of about 1.7M);
- direct rustc link: 7 s; low 22,156,668;
- program run: 53 s; low 25,023,560.

The window's minimum was 22,156,668, so the 15,728,640 notice line was never approached.

Lesson: a plain --lib build draws about 1.7M, far less than R-LIB8's 5.14M test build. For the next Legal --lib-class row, propose a floor near 22M with this evidence rather than 25.1M. Fable2 rules each one; this was a one-off.
